Source: jeyboard
Section: gnome
Priority: optional
Maintainer: John Ramsden <johnramsden@riseup.net>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), gjs
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: gnome-shell-extension-jeyboard
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, gnome-shell (>= 50~), gnome-shell (<< 52~)
Description: on-screen keyboard with real modifier keys for GNOME Shell
 A floating on-screen keyboard drawn inside GNOME Shell. Ctrl, Alt and Shift
 toggle like held hardware keys; Super is a toggle that sends a chord or a tap.
 Designed to also work on the lock screen, the login screen and in shell
 password dialogs. Intended for mouse-only (accessibility) use on Wayland.
